{"id": "sevt_01VwYz32pryHLpsDUkR353pn", "content": [{"text": "Cart's p99 jumped from about 75 ms to about 3,700 ms at 14:43, right after cart deploy `df06e76` at 14:43:20. The checkout deploy at 14:41 and the auth deploy at 14:44:50 don't fit the timing.\n\n- **Diff:** `df06e76` (\"price cart lines individually\") replaced one batched `sku_id IN (...)` query in `price_cart` with a `SkuPrice` query for each cart line. This is the N+1 pattern from the runbook's known-causes list.\n- **Log:** the batched `sku_id IN (?)` query appears 391 times. The per-row `sku_id = ?` query appears 1,888 times. Only the log's first three `sku_prices` lines (14:00) were read, all batched; the per-row count wasn't split by time.\n\nI didn't check `db_pool_utilization` or the per-request query counts after the deploy.\n\n**Root cause:** `df06e76` \u2014 `price_cart` now runs one `sku_prices` query per cart line instead of a single batched `IN` query, so each cart request makes many sequential DB round trips. Reverting it, or restoring the batched query, should fix it.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:51:38.552820Z", "type": "agent.message"}
